{
 "method": "Generated 200 photon interaction events using a simplified Monte Carlo approach, representing potential interactions within the scoring volume. Photon energies were sampled from the specified lines (1.1732 MeV and 1.3325 MeV) with equal probability. Interaction processes (Compton, photoelectric, pair production, Rayleigh) were selected based on approximate probabilities for MeV energies in water. For each process, parameters were sampled using simplified models: Compton scattering used simplified kinematics, photoelectric effect ejected an electron with kinetic energy approximately equal to the incident photon energy, pair production created an electron-positron pair, and Rayleigh scattering resulted in an elastically scattered photon. Electron and photon scattering angles were sampled using a forward-biased distribution. This simulation does not include detailed photon transport through the phantom to determine the actual probability of interaction within the defined scoring volume; instead, it samples interaction types and parameters based on energy-dependent cross-section approximations.",
